Date: Tue, 02 Dec 2014 11:35:02 +0000
Subject: Raising Likelihood to a power
Message-ID: <VgmsRYf48Xc.G4xGE1FkM3IJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-users/c/VgmsRYf48Xc/m/G4xGE1FkM3IJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi all,

I need the likelihood to be raised to a certain power (multiplied by itself)

in stan my current likelihood is defined by

y ~ multi_normal_cholesky(X*beta,L);

Does anyone know an easy way to accomplish this within the stan architecture?

Thanks for any help

Sam

From u2a7f346506a3e9ff at groups.google.com  Tue Dec  2 13:16:21 2014
From: u2a7f346506a3e9ff at groups.google.com (Marcus Brubaker)
Date: Tue, 02 Dec 2014 13:16:21 +0000
Subject: Re: [stan-users] Raising Likelihood to a power
Message-ID: <VgmsRYf48Xc.FGtWfosyLiIJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <VgmsRYf48Xc.G4xGE1FkM3IJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
References: <VgmsRYf48Xc.G4xGE1FkM3IJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-users/c/VgmsRYf48Xc/m/FGtWfosyLiIJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

This:

  increment_log_prob(p*multi_normal_cholesky_log(y,X*beta,L));

will raise your likelihood to whatever power p you want.

Cheers,
Marcus

