lp__ is being reported as jumping to and sticking at -Inf. It's not obvious to me how such a value could occur other than by overflow, but the parameters that give this value don't look dramatically different from those in earlier iterations, where lp__ was on the order of 4 x 10^{-2}, I think.

Calling log_prob from R seg faults, unfortunately.

I wonder whether it's a memory allocation problem? I noticed that the amount of memory being used by R when running this code (as reported by top in Ubuntu) was increasing rapidly, from about 7.5% around 10 minutes after starting the run, to about 77% after almost 2 hours (I didn't see how much memory was being used just before the end of the run, which took a bit less than 2.5h).

