data from this thread and failed.  The last rdump

  coralsimexplanatory.Rdata

was missing

  objects not found: z, min_y, max_y

NUTS shouldn't be able to jump to a -inf value because the Metropolis
accept step should reject a -inf value.

Is the jump always during warmup?

Memory for an iteration only depends on the size of the
expression graph and that memory gets reused, so it shouldn't
grow dramatically over the run.

I'm pretty sure RStan preallocates the space it needs for results,
so that also shouldn't be causing a jump.

I have no idea why calling log_prob() from R would seg fault --- any
seg fault caused by RStan is a bug.  If you have a reproducible example,
you (or I) can open an issue on the RStan issue tracker.  Unless there's
a reproducible example, there won't be any traction to try and fix it.

- Bob

